And who are you?

263
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:45,797
My name is Izzy Izumi, and I
came all the way from Japan.

264
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,017
And this is my Digidestined friend, Kari.

265
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,020
Hi, guys.

266
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,537
This is our friend, Jackie.

267
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:53,997
He was sent here to help us out
in case we got into trouble.

268
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:57,197
And you three guys are the
Digidestined children of Hong Kong.

269
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,110
No, we're not.

270
00:16:58,193 --> 00:16:59,117
We're the Poi Brothers.

271
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:02,257
I know this is quite a shock,
but believe me, it's all true.

272
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:04,457
We're herding the lost
Digimon into Kulong Park

273
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:06,997
so we can return them
safely to the digital world.

274
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,197
Won't you please join us?

275
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,110
What do you say?

276
00:17:09,193 --> 00:17:10,077
Huddle up, guys.

277
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,219
What do you think?

278
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:15,217
I say we join them so afterwards I can
ask the Japanese girl out on a date.

279
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:16,130
No fair.

280
00:17:16,213 --> 00:17:17,120
I saw her first.

281
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:18,197
She likes me.

282
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,515
How can you not tell?

283
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:20,990
Break!

284
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,237
All right, we've decided
to work together with Kari.

285
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:24,261
I mean the team.

286
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:25,790
Prodigis.

287
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:27,040
Thank you.

288
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,030
Uh-huh.

289
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:31,790
Ah!

290
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:44,737
The Digidestined and their Digimon are
starting to arrive from all over Asia.

291
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:46,644
I don't think Jackie heard you.

292
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,597
And one, and two, and three,
and four, and five, and...

293
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:51,037
It looks like we'll get this
over with before dinner.

294
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:51,950
So that means...

295
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:56,078
We'll get to take Kari out for the
best Hong Kong meal she's ever had.

296
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:57,290
Huh!

297
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:58,777
Bad news, Izzy?

298
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:01,477
It's an email from a girl
named Mina who lives in India.

299
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,697
I'll explain everything
later, but right now,

300
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:06,309
we've got to get to
the China-India border.

301
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,480
Excuse me, guys.

302
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,197
Can one of you please come with me?

303
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:10,157
Sure, I'll do it.

304
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,070
What's the problem?

305
00:18:11,153 --> 00:18:12,688
What should we do, Meramon?

306
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,237
I'm not sure.

307
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,997
It seems that they think
that we're the enemy.

308
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:21,786
If we try to cross the border
into China, we might start a war.

309
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:25,140
What now, General? I'm not sure.

310
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:27,977
I've never stopped monsters
from crossing our border before.

311
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:28,890
Huh?

312
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:29,921
What is it, sir?

313
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:30,890
More monsters?

314
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:32,240
This time, by air.

315
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:34,950
Hi.

316
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,557
Thanks for coming.

317
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:37,470
No problem.

318
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:39,057
Don't worry about a thing, kids.

319
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:42,117
Mega Kabuterimon and I will
hold off the Chinese army.

320
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:45,797
Right, and while we keep them
busy, get the others to Hong Kong.

321
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:47,277
Wait, it's not that easy.

322
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,297
This situation calls for diplomacy.

323
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:51,237
The last thing we want to do is cause an

324
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,617
international incident
that results in a war.

325
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,097
But what choice do we have?

326
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,617
I guess we have to explain it to them.

327
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:57,977
I don't want to go through that again.

328
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:58,977
Uh, Kari, you do it.

329
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,560
Why me? Oh, I'll do it.

330
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,617
It's probably better if a Digimon
explains it to them anyway.

331
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:06,217
But the problem is, if
we approach, they attack.

332
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,300
That's a problem.

333
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:11,560
Hey, I've got a great
idea. They're attacking.

334
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,877
Looks like one of them has a blow dryer.

335
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,725
If it's a fight they
want, then they've got it.

336
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:20,050
Spartan Age!

337
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,017
Watch your spelling, Octamon.

338
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:26,041
There's going to be a quiz later.

339
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:27,050
Huh?

340
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:29,120
We come in peace?

341
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:32,812
Sergeant, I think we've landed
in the middle of a B-movie.

342
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,915
Only one thing to do.

343
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,557
This isn't going to
look good on my resume.

344
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,470
No, sir.

345
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,849
Let's keep this maneuver
our little secret.

346
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,480
We parked! Great.

347
00:19:47,660 --> 00:19:50,597
Now let's explain our situation
to them and get to Hong Kong.

348
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,510
Right on.

349
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:01,298
I'm sure it's a good idea
to let them cross, General.

350
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:02,950
Yes.

351
00:20:03,033 --> 00:20:06,137
We're all part of the same army
when it comes to saving the world.

352
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:08,037
All right, everyone, settle down.

353
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,238
We're almost ready.

354
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,272
Kari, let's get started.

355
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:13,622
Digiport, open!

356
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,037
Thanks, everyone, for all your help.

357
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,397
Now that we're finished, why
don't I show you around town?

358
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:34,757
I think the Poi Brothers
have a crush on you, Kari.

359
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,497
Hey, why are you the one that
gets to shake Kari's hand?

360
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:38,410
Hello there.

361
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,160
You're too young!

362
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,510
Hey, come on!

363
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:04,030
Hi, mister.

364
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:05,697
I guess you're all alone, too.

365
00:21:05,780 --> 00:21:06,610
Do you wanna be friends?

366
00:21:06,693 --> 00:21:07,720
Let's go.

367
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:41,652
It's time for me to connect with my hand.

368
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:45,440
I'm going to drive together with my hand.

369
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,037
I'm going to drive together with my hand.

370
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,897
Why can't I connect with my hand?

371
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:57,177
Why can't I connect

372
00:21:57,260 --> 00:22:02,680
with my hand?

373
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:08,540
I'm always going to go,
and I'm going to fly away.

374
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:16,580
I'm always going to go, and
I'm always going to be there.

375
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:21,880
I'm always going to be one person.

376
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:49,240
The End

377
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,480
Thank you.
